sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant B as Node that starts,<br/>empty or from its disk
    participant N as Neighbours it asks
    participant L as A neighbour that listed<br/>the highest position
    Note over B: lookup of its own id over: of the closest nodes it knows,<br/>max(k/2, 10) spread across the tree,<br/>one per IP address
    par to each neighbour asked
        loop page after page, while more follow
            B->>N: ListKeys(after the last key received)
            N-->>B: KeyList: key, position, SHA-256 of the keys<br/>B should hold, one datagram
        end
    end
    Note over N: one page at a time, whoever asks:<br/>a request that comes meanwhile gets no answer
    Note over B: per key, the highest position listed,<br/>only if B lacks it or holds a lower one,<br/>the keys listed by more neighbours first
    loop at most 4 at once, 2 per neighbour, within 30 s
        B->>L: FindValue(key)
        L-->>B: its record, or nothing
        alt it hashes to the entry, is in the tree at that position<br/>and its signature verifies
            rect rgba(47, 143, 78, 0.10)
            Note over B: written by the rules of a replica
            end
        else not shown, or not the record listed
            rect rgba(201, 138, 27, 0.10)
            Note over B: the next neighbour that listed it,<br/>then a lower position, else a republication brings it
            Note over B: a neighbour that twice holds nothing<br/>for a key it listed is asked for no more records
            end
        end
    end
